implementationPlan.description:
Make an approvalMode switch reach the in-memory SPEED timers, and test it.
(a) packages/moe-daemon/src/state/profileRollout.ts, function updateProjectSettings.
- Import { clearAllSpeedModeTimeouts, rearmSpeedModeApprovals } from '../tools/submitPlan.js'. StateManager.ts:74 and taskStore.ts:37 already import from that module, and submitPlan.ts value-imports neither StateManager nor profileRollout (checked), so this adds no cycle. Do NOT edit submitPlan.ts.
- Insert the switch right after `state.project = updated;` (the successful write) and before `state.emit({ type: 'SETTINGS_UPDATED' ... })`:
  const fromMode = project.settings.approvalMode ?? 'CONTROL';
  const toMode = settings.approvalMode ?? 'CONTROL';
  if (toMode !== fromMode) {
    if (toMode === 'CONTROL') clearAllSpeedModeTimeouts();
    else if (toMode === 'SPEED') rearmSpeedModeApprovals(state);
  }
- Write a 4-line comment saying why:
  - leaving for CONTROL cancels every armed timer, because the timer re-checks only status (submitPlan.ts:127-128), never the mode;
  - entering SPEED arms pending rows with the daemon-start rule (bound revision, remaining delay counted from planSubmittedAt, armed rows skipped);
  - TURBO keeps armed timers, since it approves anyway.
- The ?? 'CONTROL' default matches setTaskStatus.ts:156.
- rearmSpeedModeApprovals reads state.project, so it must run after the assignment. It never throws: unreadable rows are recorded per row. Neither call can undo the write.
(b) New packages/moe-daemon/src/state/approvalModeSwitch.test.ts. Copy the harness from src/tools/automaticApprovalRevision.test.ts:20-60: boot(row, approvalMode) with speedModeDelayMs 50, submit() via submitPlanTool, taskActivity(), and afterEach running clearAllSpeedModeTimeouts() plus vi.useRealTimers(). Use vi.useFakeTimers({ toFake: ['setTimeout','clearTimeout'] }) and await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(ms). Cases:
  (s1) SPEED: submit, then h.state.updateSettings({ approvalMode: 'CONTROL' }), then advance 200 ms. The row is still AWAITING_APPROVAL and has no PLAN_AUTO_APPROVED event.
  (s2) CONTROL: submit (no timer), then updateSettings({ approvalMode: 'SPEED' }). The row is still AWAITING_APPROVAL before the delay, and after advancing past it the row is WORKING with exactly one PLAN_AUTO_APPROVED event and approvedPlanRevision equal to its submitted planRevision.
  (s3) SPEED: submit, switch to 'TURBO', then back to 'SPEED'. vi.getTimerCount() stays 1, and after the delay there is exactly one PLAN_AUTO_APPROVED event.
  (s4) SPEED: submit, then a setting change that leaves the mode alone (updateSettings({ chatEnabled: false })). The armed timer still approves the row. This guards against clearing on every write.
  (s5) SPEED: submit, then switch to 'TURBO'. The armed timer still approves (the documented choice).
With the hook reverted, s1 and s2 must fail.
